sentences.t:
Sparserat et latices simulatos fontis Averni,
falcibus et messae ad lunam quaeruntur aënis
pubentes herbae nigri cum lacte veneni;

sentences.l:
She had sprinkled, too, imitated waters of the Avernian spring,
and cut by the moon with bronze sickles are sought
swelling herbs with the milk of black poison;
